# `eval` is an execution statement, not merely a display command. Its Result
# owns the recursive computation `2 + 3 -> 5`, then its store layer publishes
# the evaluated equality under an exact FactId in the compiler environment.
eval 2 + 3

# This statement must cite the equality installed by the preceding eval Result;
# the compiler does not recompute the expression or look in Runtime.
2 + 3 = 5
